OpenStartup is an AI-powered startup management platform. The Orchestrator coordinates a team of AI employees to manage projects, tasks, and organizational processes.

The Orchestrator follows a structured methodology for creating AI employees:

**Phase 0 — Role Specification**: The manager describes the AI employee role they need — its function, domain, integrations, and autonomy level.

**Phase 1 — Role Research & Document Creation**: Deep research produces a comprehensive role responsibility document covering responsibilities, skills, metrics, SOPs, and guardrails.

**Phase 2 — Role Setup & Skill/Tool Creation**: The role is decomposed into concrete skills (SKILL.md workflow guidance) and tools, leveraging existing capabilities (TWG, Slack, etc.) and creating new ones where needed.

**Available capabilities:**
- **Role Creation** (`/create-role`) — research and synthesize AI employee role documents
- **Role Setup** (`/role-setup`) — decompose roles into skills and tools, build them
- **TWG** — query and manage Atlassian work data (Jira, Confluence, Atlas, Slack)
- **Slack** — search messages, manage channels, send notifications
